# Aethora lore lock

The curated lore in `docs/terminology.md` and `docs/lore/` is the leading truth for **Brightcall**.

## Before any lore or GDD change

1. **Conflict check first (mandatory).** Compare the request to `docs/terminology.md`, `docs/lore/`, and this rule. If anything **conflicts**, **disagrees**, or would **rename / retire / reverse** a locked fact: **stop**. Do **not** edit yet. List each conflict in chat (old lock → proposed change → why it matters) and wait for Dirk's call. A "master blueprint," paste, or full rewrite does **not** skip this step.
2. Only after conflicts are resolved (or Dirk says overwrite) may you edit. Compatible additions and non-conflicting expansions may proceed.
3. **Full-doc consistency pass (mandatory after any approved lore change).** Before commit, search and align **all** of: `docs/terminology.md`, `docs/lore/**`, `docs/factions/**`, `docs/gdd/**`, `docs/README.md`, `site/src/content/**`, related site pages, and `.cursor/rules/aethora-lore-lock.mdc`. No leftover retired names, no one-file-only updates, no half-applied locks.
4. Write **English only** in all docs, even if the user prompt is in another language.
5. **Overwrite** outdated paragraphs once a change is approved. Do not annotate corrections. Do not keep "formerly called X" or "do not call it Y" in narrative.
6. Affirmative prose only: state what the world **is**.
7. Forget retired names in story text. Legacy words live only in terminology's retired list.

## Locked pillars (summary)

- Game: **Brightcall** (one word)
- Genre: **Bright-punk** — between fantasy and sci-fi; modern-gloomy steampunk cousin; extreme high contrast; Sin City read (Bone/Ash/Greige + Magenta/Cyan/Gold Chroma). Master plate: `site/public/art/hero-harvester.png`
- Hard tech limit: **no** computers, screens, LEDs, internet, or modern firearms; Bright energy (bright white) or Chroma (volatile neon)
- **Brilliance:** rare cast-to-fit; **Kardia/Vesper body budget:** one full arm + shoulder + one glove on the other hand
- World: **Aethora** · Anomaly: **The Bright** (vast **cube**)
- **Eclipse / Umbra / Exit:** Null-Flint harvest or destroy only → Stitching
- **Seams / Enhancement / Bloom / Splinter-Crush:** burst + continuous weep; wraps; Bloom internal-only; Enhancement tiers (Weak/Moderate/Ultimate) are **table language only**, not lore nouns — enhancements vary a lot in the world
- **Bright cells:** bright-white charge (cyan is Chroma)
- Quantum / lab Seam model: **still in progress** — do not lock
- **House Kardia:** large former Bright-order superpower; Brightsmith craft remains; Aureate took control
- **Aureate:** former Kardia; barons/crime lords; syndicate methods; Chroma-fuel; **controlled-Bloom infantry**; heavier metal
- **Refract Labs:** Splinter-Crush weaponizers
- **Lumari:** divine spiritualists; excess Bloom
- **Penumbra:** Bright unnatural; look down on dependence; **leverage Bloomed cells/bodies** (method open) — no "Voice"
- **the Oru:** Indigenous Wardens (faction); Null-Flint; anti-harvest; natural harmony; opposite of Penumbra. Race **Oru** is broader — city Oru exist; Vesper is Oru in Kardia and stands out; Harvester work conflicts with warden ideology without requiring the word traitor
- Eras: First Light → Traveling Light → Resting Light
- Match mutation: Splintered · No Weld
- Retired: Brightforged; **Kho'Lan** (faction is **the Oru**); Adumbra; Vertex/Axiom Labs; Altered Humans; cyan Bright-cell charge; locked third-quantum-field model; The Voice; the Syndicate as faction name

